      "writtenOn": "2022-05-19T06:31:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "https://clang.llvm.org/extra/clang-tidy/checks/misc-definitions-in-headers.html#misc-definitions-in-headers is the description for this particular warning. It\u0027s particularly concerning because it can lead to potential ODR violations in some cases.\n\nThat said, can you share specific instances here where this diagnostic is being issued for this file? Maybe they would prefer to update those instances to be inline (or change how they are declaring/defining those constants instead).",
      "revId": "2ce6e0e460e31d390823863b8c87c32c874f0fe9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fef11ad9_139a6867",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1052399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-19T19:12:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This misc-definitions-in-headers warning seems useful enough\nthat it should not be disable globally.\nHowever, it also issues warnings to C/C++ code\nthat define constexpr or simple const values in .h files.\nIronically, it does not complain about macros. \n\n  make tidy-frameworks-av-media_subset\n\nwill produce about 442 or 443 warnings in MediaCodecConstatns.h.\nAll of them are constexpr with simple integer or string values.\nSo unless some funny code taking address of those constexpr,\nor really hacking on different definitions,\nit should be okay to ignore warning on those constexpr.",
      "parentUuid": "68313c5f_e0c9d5cb",
      "revId": "2ce6e0e460e31d390823863b8c87c32c874f0fe9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c63e5056_58fca92e",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1010056
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-20T18:08:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is there a preferred way for headers to actually define reusable constants that this diagnostic won\u0027t complain about? Without that, I can\u0027t see keeping this diagnostic on at all (even if it provides value about other definitions). The false positives here are staggering to me. FWIW, the document I mentioned says \"internal linkage variable definitions are ignored for now.\" to keep the false positive rate down. https://cs.android.com/android-llvm/toolchain/llvm-project/+/master:clang-tools-extra/test/clang-tidy/misc-definitions-in-headers.hpp;l\u003d179 even has the specific case of using constexpr like here. Why does this trigger diagnostics in this case?",
      "parentUuid": "fef11ad9_139a6867",
      "revId": "2ce6e0e460e31d390823863b8c87c32c874f0fe9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3cd41ca1_85884197",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1052399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-23T19:47:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The test case in misc-definitions-in-headers.hpp works because that\nconstexpr is not in a namespace.\nMediaCodecConstants.h got the warnings for all its constexpr in\nan anonymous namespace.\n\nThe documentation of misc-definitions-in-headers said that\nalthough with low risk of ODR violation, it will not give\nwarnings to constexpr in header files.\nSo we may claim that the implementation should also not give\nwarnings in MediaCodecConstants.h.\n\nThis tidy check also gives warnings for function definitions in headers,\nand find quite a few error-prone places in AOSP.\nSo, it is useful to enable it globally.\n\nUntil it is changed to allow constexpr in anonymous namespaces,\nthe few android header files with this case can either suppress this\ncheck with NOLINTBEGIN/NOLINTEND, or remove anonymous namespaces.",
      "parentUuid": "c63e5056_58fca92e",
      "revId": "2ce6e0e460e31d390823863b8c87c32c874f0fe9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
